Regression cases for the CLAIRE4 Go compiler
============================================

Each case is a self-contained module that used to make "claire4 -cm" fail,
or generate wrong code. They are small on purpose: they were extracted from
the port of choco, where the same bugs were hidden inside 9 500 lines.

The module name is declared in init.cl and must be given on the command line
(the directory names contain '-' and cannot be used as module names):

    cd gany-arithmetic
    claire4 -cm GanyArithmetic
    ./bin/ganyarithmetic

(The generated files -- <Module>/, <Module>.go, go.work, bin/ -- are ignored
by test/regress/.gitignore.)


Cases
-----

gany-arithmetic/     reading a global declared ":any" gave a malformed EID,
                     so "GANY + 1" returned 1 instead of 42.
                     CLAIRE3 returns 42.   Fixed (commit 8f52490).

        [known bug] the generated binary prints 42 for all three probes.

rangecheck-status/   a method whose body is typed but not exact ends with
                     RangeCheck, which can raise [17]. Such a method must be
                     marked exception-ready, otherwise its callers generate a
                     native function that consumes an EID:
                         F_getPb_void() + 1   (mismatched types EID and int)
                     Fixed (commit 7b994db).

        [known bug] getPb = 41, useIt = 42.

do-division/         OPEN. Dividing the result of a function that may throw
                     still fails to build:
                         cannot use try_2 (Kernel.EID) as int value
                     "probe" is generated as a native function although it
                     calls getF(), which may raise. This is the last error
                     left when compiling choco (Choco/search.go:1173,
                     getBestVal(MidValHeuristic) -> x.inf + (x.sup - x.inf)/2).

        [known bug] the build fails; it is the purpose of the test.

        Root cause, in compile/osystem.cl (g_throw1, branch Call_method):
            if (self.arg = m_unsafe | notOpt(self) = false | ...) false
            else if g_throw(self.args) true
        notOpt(/ by a non-zero literal) is false, so the first branch answers
        "no throw" without ever looking at the operands. getF() may raise: the
        division is safe, its operand is not.

        Fixing this by testing the arguments first repairs do-division but
        breaks choco at source/var.cl:164:
            [141] list<any>(dom, EID, "try_28", true, false) is a wrong arg
                  list for Generate/g_statement
        i.e. g_statement/g_try do not yet support an expression that becomes
        throwing where it was not. Both sides must be fixed together -- see
        TODO-CLAIRE4.md, "Analyse complete du dernier bug".


How they were found
-------------------

All three were first diagnosed on choco:

    gany-arithmetic     CURRENT_PB:any := unknown  (source/model.cl)
    rangecheck-status   [choco/getActiveProblem() : Problem -> CURRENT_PB]
                        used as getActiveProblem().propagationEngine
    do-division         [getBestVal(vh:MidValHeuristic, x:IntVar) : integer
                          -> x.inf + (x.sup - x.inf) / 2]      (source/search.cl)

Comparing with CLAIRE3 (cclaire from xlclaire-v3.7.8) is what proved that the
":any" case was a CLAIRE4 regression and not a quirk of the program.
